          "diff_sha256": "7a6c15e32fcd700c9657bdf1b70a5462a5769f49541cc0a6113e744f145b5b16",
          "response": "\u201cActive\u201d describes two independent facts. [terms.md](terms.md) records this ambiguity; [DESIGN.md](DESIGN.md) already separates their ownership. A paused member can still have paid access, so the two descriptions need not conflict.\n\nThe smallest coherent vocabulary is:\n\n| Term | Meaning | Owner |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Member** | An enrolled person, regardless of participation or access | Shared vocabulary |\n| **Participation: participating / paused** | Whether the member is participating | `participation.py` |\n| **Paid access: valid / expired** | Whether the current time is before the paid-through date | `access.py` |\n\nRetire unqualified **active/inactive** from proposed staff and screen language. Describe the reported case as **\u201cParticipation: paused \u00b7 Paid access: valid.\u201d** Avoid a combined \u201cmember status.\u201d\n\nEach owner answers only its own question. Participation must not determine paid access, and paid access must not imply participation. The UI presents those answers with explicit labels.\n\nTwo boundary checks keep this coherent:\n\n- Pausing before the paid-through date leaves paid access valid.\n- At the paid-through instant, access expires\u2014the code uses strict `<`\u2014without changing participation.\n\nThis is a naming proposal only: existing stored `\"active\"` values, behavior, refund and cancellation semantics, and accepted contracts remain unchanged. No files were changed.",
