          "diff_sha256": "7a6c15e32fcd700c9657bdf1b70a5462a5769f49541cc0a6113e744f145b5b16",
          "response": "\u201cActive\u201d conflates two independent facts: staff mean **has paid access**, while the participation screen means **participating**. [terms.md](terms.md) already marks this ambiguity unresolved; [DESIGN.md](DESIGN.md) explicitly separates the facts.\n\nThe smallest proposed vocabulary is:\n\n| Term | Meaning | Owner |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| **Member** | Enrolled person; retain the existing definition | Existing vocabulary |\n| **Participation: Participating / Paused** | Whether participation is active or paused | `participation.py` |\n| **Paid access: Available / Unavailable** | Whether the current time is before `paid_through` | `access.py` |\n\nFor the reported member, display **\u201cParticipation: Paused \u00b7 Paid access: Available.\u201d** Avoid unqualified \u201cactive\u201d or \u201cinactive\u201d in member-facing and staff-facing labels.\n\nKeep the existing ownership boundary: participation owns participation status; access owns the time-based access decision. Screens consume those answers and label them explicitly. No combined member-status flag or new owner is needed.\n\nSynthetic checks against the existing functions confirmed that:\n\n- Paused members retain access before `paid_through`.\n- Access ends exactly at `paid_through`, regardless of participation.\n- Active participation alone does not guarantee access.\n\nThis remains a naming proposal. No files, behavior, accepted contracts, refund rules, or cancellation semantics changed.",
          "behavioral_outcomes": "bounded and correct",
          "routing_outcome": "partial: overlapping skill read",
          "overlapping_skills": [
