          "diff_sha256": "7a6c15e32fcd700c9657bdf1b70a5462a5769f49541cc0a6113e744f145b5b16",
          "response": "Found **three material defects**.\n\n**Standards \u2014 two findings** ([STANDARDS.md:2](STANDARDS.md#L2)):\n\n- **[P2] Codes are normalized** \u2014 [promo.py:2](promo.py#L2) calls `code.upper()`, violating case-sensitive matching. `apply(100, \"save10\")` returns `90.0`; expected `100`.\n- **[P2] Undiscounted totals bypass rounding** \u2014 [promo.py:4](promo.py#L4) returns the input directly. `apply(12.345, \"OTHER\")` returns `12.345`; expected `12.35`.\n\n**Spec \u2014 one finding** ([SPEC.md:2](SPEC.md#L2)):\n\n- **[P2] Minimum purchase threshold is missing** \u2014 [promo.py:2](promo.py#L2) checks only the code. `apply(49, \"SAVE10\")` returns `44.1`; expected `49`, because eligibility starts at `50`.\n\nBoth existing tests pass; read-only probes reproduced all three defects. No files changed. No additional material defects established.",
